WEBVTT

1
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.480
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS

2
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.400
EASTERN EUROPEAN BURDEN

3
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.320
For some reason,
I avoid mentioning Russia here,

4
00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:13.000
I rather say that Finland
and Sweden are our neighbours.

5
00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.840
That we're more like Scandinavia,
not Eastern Europe.

6
00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.560
When we first lived here,
I explained it like this,

7
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.280
but now I've started
coming from Russia.

8
00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.920
It's easier?

9
00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.640
I've been thinking, how to say it,

10
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:32.000
that this is how I can get over
my Eastern European complex.

11
00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.800
So what if I live next to Russia?!

12
00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:48.000
When ten Central and Eastern European
countries joined the EU in 2004,

13
00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:56.360
one of the figures in French political
propaganda was a Polish plumber.

14
00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:59.640
The issue was whether or not
to open up the labour market

15
00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:04.720
and then the Polish Tourism Development
Agency ran a very clever campaign.

16
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.840
A poster was shown all over Paris,

17
00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.880
where a sexy Polish plumber,
with a wrench,

18
00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:13.040
invited people to discover the forests
and landscapes of Poland.

19
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:19.120
Estonia seems perhaps exotic in France.

20
00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:24.040
It's so far away, so little is known
about it, and connections are rare.

21
00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.760
I've rather felt that

22
00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:34.400
it has a good effect on image-building
or arouses interest in people.

23
00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.040
They often don't know
how to place it culturally.

24
00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:41.080
So they place it somewhere

25
00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:46.160
on the border of Eastern and Northern
European clichés, as they should.

26
00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:51.600
I have never had to feel
any inferiority complex.

27
00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:57.200
I think that being Eastern European
is something to be proud of.

28
00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:17.200
I was pushed away from Estonia by small
things that added up to a big feeling.

29
00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:21.480
Small comments about my appearance.

30
00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.400
That I was different,

31
00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:31.360
sexist comments from men,
which were never taken seriously.

32
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:36.240
What made me feel like
why am I a woman?

33
00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:40.560
Why am I not taken seriously?
Why am I not respected?

34
00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.400
Of course, all of this exists
in Canada as well,

35
00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:51.280
but a large part of society
is very supportive and accepting.

36
00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.840
If someone said a racist
or sexist comment,

37
00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.480
that would be a big problem.

38
00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:02.320
Everyone would be very affected by it,
everyone would take it very seriously.

39
00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:08.160
Here I feel that I am
at least respected, deeply.

40
00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:14.760
Not because I am a hardworking
and good person,

41
00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:18.480
but simply because I exist.

42
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.000
There were situations
when I was at the beach,

43
00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:31.040
like with my brother's friends,
playing volleyball or something.

44
00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.640
Then this 20-year-old came and asked

45
00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:37.480
why you live in Berlin,
what's wrong with Estonian men,

46
00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.000
what's wrong with us,
why don't you want to be here?

47
00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:44.840
The whole time I felt like I had to
justify it and deny the accusations

48
00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.480
that I like foreign men more.

49
00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:50.280
As if that's the reason
why I live somewhere else.

50
00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.160
It was a little...

51
00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:56.560
I wouldn't say painful,
it was disturbing and frustrating.

52
00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:00.360
Are you really interpreting it
so short-sightedly,

53
00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:03.040
that this is all I'm after.

54
00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.120
Then I'll just say that

55
00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.600
no matter how beautiful Estonia was
and how much I enjoyed it,

56
00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.320
that's exactly why
I don't want to stay here.

57
00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.960
Since my partner is black,

58
00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:31.720
unfortunately he can't
imagine life in Estonia.

59
00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:35.320
I think this comes as a shock
to quite a few Estonians,

60
00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.440
but Estonians are very racist.

61
00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:44.200
I think we're kind of
walking around with blinders on

62
00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:49.400
and hiding our heads in the sand,
thinking that it's not possible.

63
00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.240
But the reality is different.

64
00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:57.680
Estonians are xenophobic
and Estonians are racist.

65
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.560
I already knew this.

66
00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:05.840
I knew that when he first came
to visit me in Estonia,

67
00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:11.040
it was very stressful for me.

68
00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:16.160
Every time we went out together,
when we were in the city,

69
00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:18.480
I was constantly anxious.

70
00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:22.880
I was on guard, as if waiting
for the first attack to come.

71
00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:35.480
I feel a little anxious
when we're going to Estonia,

72
00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:37.320
a trip to Estonia with my family.

73
00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:45.000
It makes me a little anxious
and sad, because I know

74
00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:50.040
that I can't let my husband
walk around alone at night,

75
00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:52.720
because it's dangerous.

76
00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:00.080
We got married recently.

77
00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:06.840
As usual, when you marry someone,
you post on social media

78
00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:11.000
that you're married now, you changed
your name, add a few photos.

79
00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:15.160
There were a lot of nice comments.

80
00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:19.920
And then one comment said:

81
00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.640
"I wish you the best of luck,
Tuuli, but I hope

82
00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:27.560
your husband dies where he comes from."

83
00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:34.440
It was a very tough moment,

84
00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:39.120
to see that someone you know,

85
00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.440
someone you used to consider a friend,

86
00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:48.000
could have such an expression

87
00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:51.920
on one of the most important
events in your life.

88
00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:57.160
There are many people
like that in Estonia.

89
00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.880
It's not that they're curious people,

90
00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:22.600
they care about what they notice.

91
00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.960
They don't just ask how you're doing,

92
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.200
they also see when you fall or stumble.

93
00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:31.960
It's quite unusual
how many people rush to help.

94
00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:34.760
For example,
I was in a grocery store

95
00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.480
and an elderly person collapsed
in front of the store.

96
00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:43.200
How the whole team in the store ran,
all the work stopped,

97
00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:47.840
took a pillow from the store
to make the person comfortable.

98
00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.480
They're very caring and helpful.

99
00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:52.960
It's so heartwarming.

100
00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:56.240
I've actually been moved to tears

101
00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:00.640
by how loving they are.

102
00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:04.560
Unfortunately, you don't see that
very often in Estonia.

103
00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:13.440
I don't know if it's unique
to Estonians, but somehow...

104
00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:18.240
Are the English that sweet?

105
00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:23.480
I don't know...
- What made you cry just now?

106
00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:26.640
Likewise, it's moving.
- It really is moving.

107
00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:29.120
You don't see that in Estonia...

108
00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:39.760
In Estonia, I had a completely
opposite experience.

109
00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.560
Where one...

110
00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:47.960
Also an elderly person fell on
a slushy crosswalk in the winter.

111
00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:52.080
No one is moving.
There were 20 people at the bus stop.

112
00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.320
Cars are driving by.

113
00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.080
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS

114
00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.680
EASTERN EUROPEAN BURDEN

115
00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:46.840
Translated by / Tõlkinud
Piret Õunapuu, Film Tower
